Sat Nov 14 08:13:36 UTC 2026 - Ackerman-00 <noreply@example.com>

- version 4.0-0
- %install: strip the payload's resources/app-update.yml and resources/package-type
  before packaging. The find line had landed after the %files file list, where rpm
  reads it as a file path and aborts with "File must begin with /", so the package
  could not be rebuilt at all.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 15:20:00 UTC 2026 - Ackerman-00 <noreply@example.com>

- version 4.0-0
- Build fix: drop the 36 dangling weather-clear-night symlinks that the
  upstream V4.0 KDE variant ships (their target weather-clear-night.svg
  does not exist), which made the RPM link check fail the build
- Build fix: locate the upstream source directory instead of a hardcoded
  Hatter-4.0 path, and run the Debian rules under bash
- Run gtk-update-icon-cache through a build-time no-op shim in the Debian
  recipe and keep it out of the Debian build dependencies: OBS could not
  resolve the package and Debian regenerates icon caches from dpkg triggers
- Add gtk-update-icon-cache (RPM: gtk3-tools) to the RPM post/postun
  requirements
- Deduplicate identical icons across the 21 theme variants with fdupes
  (the duplicated payload was 95 MB in the RPM)

